<% content_for :title, "Document and workflow automation | Norman Simplified" %>
<% content_for :description, "Examples of document and workflow automation after a Workflow Review. See a sample, possible projects, and how we agree what to measure." %>

<main class="ns-ai">
  <section class="ns-hero ns-section" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="ns-container ns-ai__hero">
      <p class="sn-eyebrow">Examples</p>
      <h1 id="ai-title" class="t-display ns-hero__title">Less manual work between your tools</h1>
      <p class="ns-lead">After a Workflow Review, we can connect the steps that slow your team down: retyping documents, chasing approvals, or keeping spreadsheets in sync. These are examples of possible work, not measured results.</p>
      <div class="ns-actions">
        <%= link_to "Request a call", studio_contact_path(interest: "audit"), data: { controller: "analytics", action: "click->analytics#track", analytics_event_param: "cta_clicked", analytics_cta_param: "request_a_call", analytics_location_param: "hero", analytics_interest_param: "audit" }, class: "sn-btn sn-btn--primary sn-btn--lg" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <%= render "studio/pages/explorer" %>
  <section class="ns-section ns-ai__explanation" aria-labelledby="build-shape">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 class="t-heading" id="build-shape">One process, connected to your tools</h2></header>
      <div class="ns-prose">
        <p>A Pilot starts at $18,000 and takes 3–4 weeks. A Full integration starts at $36,000 and takes 6–8 weeks. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins. We agree what to measure before kickoff and scope one process at a time.</p>
        <p>The usual first step is a Workflow Review: $4,500 fixed fee, two weeks. You get a recommended first change and a budget range, then decide whether to continue.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <%= render "studio/pages/catalog" %>
  <section class="ns-section ns-ai__explanation" aria-labelledby="human-review">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 class="t-heading" id="human-review">A person sees the exceptions</h2></header>
      <div class="ns-prose">
        <p>The model proposes. It does not get the last word on a low-confidence field or on an action you mark as sensitive: sending a message, moving money, changing a customer record.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>You and I set the confidence line and the sensitive actions before launch</li>
          <li>Items under the line go to a named role on your team</li>
          <li>The reviewer sees the source document next to the field</li>
          <li>Nothing reaches the system your team uses until the rule for that field says it can</li>
          <li>Overrides are stored, so the next review is not from memory</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="ns-section ns-ai__explanation" aria-labelledby="evals">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 class="t-heading" id="evals">Accuracy is measured on your documents</h2></header>
      <div class="ns-prose">
        <p>I don't publish a universal accuracy number. Before go-live I label a sample from your files and score the workflow against it. You see the misses, not a vendor benchmark.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The sample is documents you recognize</li>
          <li>The score is per field, not one flattering average</li>
          <li>That set stays as a check we repeat when a prompt or model changes</li>
          <li>If the sample is too small or too clean to trust, I say so before you rely on it</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="ns-section ns-ai__explanation" aria-labelledby="running-costs">
    <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
      <header class="ns-section-heading"><h2 class="t-heading" id="running-costs">The model bill is a line item, not a surprise</h2></header>
      <div class="ns-prose">
        <p>AI usage cost depends on document length, how many fields you extract, and monthly volume. I estimate it from your real volume before build, set a monthly ceiling, and alert when spend approaches it. There is no honest dollar figure for that bill until those inputs exist.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>You pay the model provider, or I pass the cost through with the ceiling written down</li>
          <li>Retries and long documents are part of the estimate</li>
          <li>After launch, Ongoing operations support starts at $6,500 a month: monitoring, updates to the checks, the cost cap, and a one-page note on what changed. Your written proposal sets the fixed fee before work begins</li>
          <li>You can run it yourself with the handoff notes if you prefer</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
